Subject: virt-aa-helper: complete partial backing chain metadata

Origin: Nex recovery S0 native probe, 2026-09-25
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, as in src/security/virt-aa-helper.c

When domain XML specifies only a prefix of a disk's backing chain, probe from
the last explicit source so AppArmor grants read access to the remaining
backing files. An explicit empty backingStore remains a terminator and is not
probed past. Keep the existing total chain-depth limit when probing a suffix.
---
 src/security/virt-aa-helper.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/src/security/virt-aa-helper.c
+++ b/src/security/virt-aa-helper.c
@@ -887,5 +887,7 @@ get_files(vahControl * ctl)
     for (i = 0; i < ctl->def->ndisks; i++) {
         virDomainDiskDef *disk = ctl->def->disks[i];
+        virStorageSource *backing;
+        size_t depth = 1;
 
         if (virStorageSourceIsEmpty(disk->src))
             continue;
@@ -893,7 +895,10 @@ get_files(vahControl * ctl)
          * implementation.
          */
-        if (!disk->src->backingStore)
-            virStorageSourceGetMetadata(disk->src, -1, -1, 200, false);
+        for (backing = disk->src; virStorageSourceIsBacking(backing->backingStore);
+             backing = backing->backingStore, depth++)
+            ;
+        if (!backing->backingStore && depth <= 200)
+            virStorageSourceGetMetadata(backing, -1, -1, 201 - depth, false);
 
          /* XXX should handle open errors more careful than just ignoring them.
          */
